<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:05:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>France: Student anger rages as tear gas and fires hit Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-student-anger-rages-as-tear-gas-and-fires-hit-paris</link><description>
Around 480,000 people took part in nationwide student demonstrations across France on Tuesday, according to student and school unions, up from the previous week’s mobilisation. In Paris, the demonstration ended with tear gas and fires, as tensions escalated. Claire Paccalin has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c583610a-c71d-11f1-953b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-173108-173500-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c583610a-c71d-11f1-953b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-173108-173500-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca6d2ade-c71d-11f1-a902-cb0f39029e6a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:03:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>From Paris to Marseille, high school protests continue across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-from-paris-to-marseille-high-school-protests-continue-across-france</link><description>
Student protests continue across France, with marches taking place in cities including Lille and Marseille while pupils in Paris stage fresh school blockades using wheelie bins. Demonstrators are calling for better learning conditions, saying government measures announced so far have failed to address their concerns. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a618d84-c71a-11f1-96ba-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/minimanif.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a618d84-c71a-11f1-96ba-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/minimanif.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5322f998-c71a-11f1-aadf-31245b2721cf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:40:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In Kenya, recycled plastic gets a second life as chess pieces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces</link><description>
In Nairobi, a project is helping children develop focus, patience and critical thinking through chess, using pieces made from recycled plastic waste.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a99973e-c718-11f1-9dfa-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-225312-225439-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a99973e-c718-11f1-9dfa-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-225312-225439-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fa1c26a-c718-11f1-90b1-1b19ca1118fa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:28:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France in focus</category><title>Broken children: France confronts crisis of sexual violence against minors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261013-broken-children-france-confronts-crisis-of-sexual-violence-against-minors</link><description>
In France, a new "comprehensive law" aims to strengthen preventative measures, the judicial process and support for child victims of sexual violence. Yet advocacy groups, lawyers, and healthcare professionals point out that the legislation has numerous shortcomings. We take a closer look in this edition of France in Focus. Warning: viewers may find parts of this report disturbing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/075a50da-c6d7-11f1-b929-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PIC-2-CEF-VIOLENCES-SEXUELLES-MINEURS-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/075a50da-c6d7-11f1-b929-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PIC-2-CEF-VIOLENCES-SEXUELLES-MINEURS-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">376f86c2-c6dd-11f1-af70-75b97fc69acf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:24:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Aurore Cloé DUPUIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French youth demand answers as education protests enter third week</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-youth-demand-answers-as-education-protests-enter-third-week</link><description>
French students have continued nationwide protests for a third week, demanding more funding for education, better teaching conditions and more staff. The government’s plan to recruit 3,000 substitute teachers has failed to satisfy demonstrators, who are calling for an additional €10 billion in education spending. Backed by teachers and unions, protesters warn the mobilisation will continue as the government prepares budget cuts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/acc0217e-c715-11f1-9f1c-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-163631-163805-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/acc0217e-c715-11f1-9f1c-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-163631-163805-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1d7c69e-c715-11f1-86ad-e9e3444e4d54</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:18:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish royals visit Ceuta amid tensions with Morocco over migrant influx</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx</link><description>
Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time in 14 years on Tuesday, as the North African enclave grapples with the aftermath of a mass migrant influx. Authorities have cleared makeshift camps from the beaches ahead of the visit, amid strained relations with neighbouring Morocco.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed7deb02-c714-11f1-8a12-33956213bea6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:17:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg">© Manu Fernandez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications amid renewed anti-immigrant protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests</link><description>
Tensions have flared in South Africa after a court ruling prompted the government to open its application system to all foreign nationals, regardless of their legal status. Despite applications remaining subject to approval, anti-immigrant protests erupted outside several Home Affairs offices, forcing authorities to temporarily suspend refugee and asylum applications. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e81674a6-c717-11f1-bdd1-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224920-225113-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e81674a6-c717-11f1-bdd1-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224920-225113-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eda485a2-c717-11f1-97e6-5f5703cb1bba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:15:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopian forces enter key Tigray town, raising fears among residents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents</link><description>
Ethiopian federal forces and their allies have entered a key town in northern Tigray near the Eritrean border after rebel fighters withdrew. As the conflict intensifies, residents fear further violence and instability. Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeb1b5a4-c717-11f1-8351-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224604-224800-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeb1b5a4-c717-11f1-8351-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-224604-224800-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3de80d4-c717-11f1-89b4-c75f6940fd2e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:13:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency</link><description>
Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ff87552-c715-11f1-b7f0-ff2b36bbad19</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:59:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Oil facility near Yemen capital Sanaa hit by Saudi Arabia, Houthis say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261013-oil-facility-near-yemen-capital-sanaa-hit-by-saudi-arabia-houthis-say</link><description>
Houthi media reported an ​attack ‌by Saudi Arabia on ⁠the ‌Yemen Oil Company ⁠in Sanaa on Tuesday, which came ‌shortly after the ‌Saudi-led coalition ​ordered the evacuation of the ​facility ​ahead of ​a military ​operation. The Iran-backed rebels had warned that they would target Riyadh's airport and other sites in the country if Saudi Arabia followed through on its threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa990e7e-c710-11f1-9026-f5d5f270ea54</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:53:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Student protesters want to 'keep the pressure up on the government'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-student-protesters-want-to-keep-the-pressure-up-on-the-government</link><description>
Thousands of demonstrators took to the streets of Paris on Tuesday in support of high school students protesting poor classroom conditions. The mobilisation brought together not only students but also teachers, unions, political figures and activists, including Greta Thunberg, from across the country. Protesters say they want to maintain pressure on the French government, insisting their demands remain unmet. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin has the latest from the demonstration in Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbf51eca-c714-11f1-a624-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-160118-160627-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbf51eca-c714-11f1-a624-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-160118-160627-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0fe4c16-c714-11f1-b30e-db793cebe9d5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:52:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Novelist Thélyson Orélien rejects AI claims after bestseller pulled from French prize list</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261013-novelist-th%C3%A9lyson-or%C3%A9lien-rejects-ai-claims-after-book-pulled-from-french-prize-list</link><description>
Thélyson Orélien, the Haitian-Canadian writer whose best-selling debut novel was pulled from the prestigious Goncourt prize list amid an AI uproar, said Tuesday "not a single sentence" had been written by a machine. He did, however, admit to "unacceptable mistakes" regarding accusations of plagiarism involving earlier works.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/155b72fe-c713-11f1-a4a6-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2d5600857b2d465f62af369a7944e3c97aa68320.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/155b72fe-c713-11f1-a4a6-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2d5600857b2d465f62af369a7944e3c97aa68320.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16221fee-c713-11f1-b58c-f91e8853e136</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:33:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/155b72fe-c713-11f1-a4a6-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2d5600857b2d465f62af369a7944e3c97aa68320.jpg">© Joel Saget, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France votes on sexual violence bill</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-votes-on-sexual-violence-bill</link><description>
France’s National Assembly is set to vote on a comprehensive bill to tackle sexual and gender-based violence. The proposed legislation would create specialised police units to investigate sexual crimes, broaden the definition of incest, and introduce penalties for stalking and sending unsolicited explicit images. It also includes school interviews aimed at detecting abuse and violence. If adopted, the law would come into force in 2032. While the bill has broad political support, some NGOs have expressed disappointment with the final draft, arguing that key measures have been weakened or removed, as Luke Shrago explains from the National Assembly.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6bc68da-c70d-11f1-8a09-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-152645-153118-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6bc68da-c70d-11f1-8a09-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-152645-153118-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc1eedf2-c70d-11f1-8b8d-6187f58efc6f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:29:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgium: Greener schools thanks to European funding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding</link><description>
🇧🇪 In Ganshoren, in Belgium, a new school replaces run-down buildings. But the need for renovations remains enormous.👉🏻 Find the whole reporting on France 24 English. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95428516-c70e-11f1-80b7-914b699b402e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:27:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia seeks to overwhelm NATO allies with crises 'across a wide spectrum of geographic locations'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-russia-seeks-to-overwhelm-nato-allies-with-crises-across-a-wide-spectrum-of-geographic-locations</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Dr. Gavin Hall, NATO expert and Teaching Fellow in Political Science and International Security at the University of Strathclyde. NATO is sending a stark warning to Moscow: any Russian attack on alliance territory could trigger retaliation far beyond the battlefield, targeting “anything and everything that supports, sustains, and controls” the attacking force. But can Europe defend itself without Washington, as Donald Trump signals a renewed rapprochement with Russia?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caf9f266-c709-11f1-96e4-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-150403-151627-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caf9f266-c709-11f1-96e4-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-150403-151627-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d001a722-c709-11f1-a6a4-53da7ad8bc98</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:20:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Musical trailblazer Lakecia Benjamin: From chasing Prince to touring with Stevie Wonder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261013-musical-trailblazer-lakecia-benjamin-from-chasing-prince-to-touring-with-stevie-wonder</link><description>
In this interview with FRANCE 24's Culture editor Eve Jackson, saxophonist Lakecia Benjamin looks back at her distinguished career. From trying to sneak into Prince's Las Vegas shows to catching the attention of Stevie Wonder, the six-time Grammy-nominated musician has carved out a career working with some of the biggest names in music, from Missy Elliott and Jay-Z to Alicia Keys. In 2023, her album "Phoenix", recorded after a near-fatal car accident, earned three Grammy nominations and marked a turning point in her career.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b77ee20-c702-11f1-9b63-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-13-10-2026-11-59-ING18-CLEAN-N3-frame-29114.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b77ee20-c702-11f1-9b63-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-13-10-2026-11-59-ING18-CLEAN-N3-frame-29114.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">399d3962-c6fb-11f1-a765-55ed6e285468</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:14:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>French student protests: From confiscated signs to catchy slogans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261013-french-student-protests-from-confiscated-signs-to-catchy-slogans</link><description>
As French student protests continue, we take a look at how French police have seized some protest signs. We break down whether this is legal, or police intimidation. We also discuss the origin of a slogan that's catching on – "Bismillah, c'est les ténèbres" – and another that allegedly, according to Le Parisien newspaper, has made French President Emmanuel Macron furious. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbed9fca-c708-11f1-96e1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5b655143.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbed9fca-c708-11f1-96e1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5b655143.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6459855c-c70a-11f1-8ff3-fd6bccab6fab</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:05:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>French embassy in Riyadh tells citizens to avoid Saudi airports targeted by Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261013-french-embassy-in-riyadh-tells-citizens-to-avoid-saudi-airports-targeted-by-houthis</link><description>
France's embassy in Saudi Arabia told its citizens to avoid the airports in Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam on Tuesday as fighting escalates between a Saudi-led coalition and Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels, who have been attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities since last week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77d63f76-c70a-11f1-9784-3ffc75c10a41</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Preserving Lebanon's stories amid war: France's Lebanese Film Festival</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261013-preserving-lebanon-s-stories-amid-war-france-s-lebanese-film-festival</link><description>
This Tuesday evening sees the start of the sixth edition of France's Lebanese Film Festival. The festival opens at the Elysées Lincoln cinema in Paris, with Nadim Tabet's supernatural thriller "In This Darkness I See You". This year's edition will also feature a retrospective of the work of actress and director Nadine Labaki, including her Oscar-nominated film "Capernaum". In Perspective, we spoke to festival president Sarah Hajjar.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85c8a15e-c70b-11f1-a80c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d1912626.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85c8a15e-c70b-11f1-a80c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d1912626.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6e99f8e-c6fa-11f1-aa57-01559fb70d48</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:43:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia pounds Ukrainian cities, spares energy targets for first time since Trump 'ceasefire'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire</link><description>
Russia hammered Ukrainian cities and transport links overnight into Tuesday, killing at least four people in the city of Kharkiv, while appearing to spare energy facilities for the first time since US President Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire" at the weekend. It was not clear whether Moscow had deliberately avoided targeting power plants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8171a586-c703-11f1-9a3d-3b1e1fb2f193</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:39:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg">© Sofiia Gatilova, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Hope so heavy to carry': Al-Shaer on harrowing plight, emotional toll, struggle to survive in Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hope-so-heavy-to-carry-al-shaer-on-harrowing-plight-emotional-toll-struggle-to-survive-in-gaza</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Palestinian writer and poet Mahmoud Al-Shaer, “Am I real, or just a number in this war?” In I Am Still Alive: Dispatches from Gaza, Palestinian writer Mahmoud Al-Shaer explores how war transforms memory, childhood and the meaning of existence. Recounting his family's displacement, his daughter's understanding of a world reduced to tents, and his evacuation from Gaza, he reflects on writing as an act of resistance against erasure. His testimony reveals how the struggle for survival extends beyond physical destruction to the preservation of identity, collective memory and the possibility of a normal life.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9397d8a-c603-11f1-9405-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-081057-082155-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9397d8a-c603-11f1-9405-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-081057-082155-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">def42f40-c603-11f1-bc89-fb9316923bc6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:36:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French school shooting suspect linked to online group that glorifies mass killers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261013-french-school-shooting-suspect-linked-to-online-group-that-glorifies-mass-killers</link><description>
A 14-year-old pupil suspected of shooting and wounding a headmaster and teacher near Marseille may have been involved in an online network associated with the glorification of mass killers known as the True Crime Community, prompting France’s anti-terror prosecutor to take over the case.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7548a0c0-c708-11f1-a8cb-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2ZE2Y2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7548a0c0-c708-11f1-a8cb-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2ZE2Y2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc696f7c-c705-11f1-9722-85a00dc8f378</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7548a0c0-c708-11f1-a8cb-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2ZE2Y2.jpg">© Miguel Medina, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish royals visit crisis-hit Ceuta amid diplomatic tensions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions</link><description>
Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time since 2007, amid tensions with Morocco following July’s migration crisis, when more than 70,000 people crossed into the Spanish enclave. Most returned to Morocco, but thousands remained, and dozens died. Morocco claims sovereignty over Ceuta, making the royal visit diplomatically sensitive. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris has more from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97223c96-c704-11f1-ad22-ff6afdbff2d2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump’s use of Russian diesel fuel, at Ukraine’s expense, sparks controversy in the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us</link><description>
Donald Trump’s plan to import Russian diesel despite Western sanctions has sparked fierce criticism in Washington, including from Republicans, as high fuel prices and the upcoming midterm elections put pressure on his administration. His approach to the Ukraine war has also drawn controversy, with calls for Kyiv to hold elections and claims of an energy ceasefire announced without clear agreement from the parties involved. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert has the analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1588b1d0-c707-11f1-98cd-b1c2e58f18c5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:26:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
